{
 "_doc": "Per-fixture DOT node-size ratchet for the description DOT-parity suite (mission S1L). Same convention as oracle/goldens/state|object/size-backlog.json: structurally EQUAL fixtures whose maxSizeDeltaIn (inches, max across their svek-N graphs) exceeds the 0.01in conformant bar; the test asserts delta <= pinned + 1e-6 per fixture, so pins only shrink. A sub-mission that makes a fixture conformant drops its delta to <=0.01 and DELETES the entry (absent slug => conformant required). Re-baselined 2026-07-27 after S1L-b (description [ ... ] display-body expansion) from scripts/measure-description-size-deltas.ts. 115 entries / 351 goldens => 236 (67.2%) conformant. S1L-b flipped dexigu-24/kenece-24/zifaji-87 (the HR-body trio) plus butebe-90/zavitu-69 to conformant (deleted). fariba-82 is pinned 1.024479: S1L-b T6 diagnosed it as a compound residual (out-of-scope awslib sprite + a jar `file`-body word-wrap gap, S1L-d), NOT a leaf-width bug -- see plans/s1l-leaf-sizing/ledger.md. zotiru-33 shrank 2.655 -> 0.914 (S1L-b T5 wired scoped `<style> package { MinimumWidth }`; the `not_nested` package is now exact at 4.583in, residual is the nested package cluster (S1L-e) + an unclosed-`<color>` note tag). Root-cause families + sub-mission routing are in plans/s1l-leaf-sizing/ledger.md. The 2 latex fixtures are a permanent inherent-tolerance DIVERGENCE (KaTeX != JLaTeXMath, see DIVERGENCES.md), excluded from the conformant denominator but still pinned here shrink-only. S1L-b-unicode (2026-07-27) landed the codepoint decode-ordering fix (<U+..>/&#..; decode per-line at measure time, AFTER the newline split): heights no longer over-split, so gafico-37 shrank 5.680208->3.752777 and nujito-06 3.350521->3.122049 (shrink-only). Still 236/351 (67.2%) conformant -- the 3 targets remain named width residuals, NOT emoji-width bugs: gafico-37 + nujito-06 are driven by the UNPORTED <code> creole block (node c, deferred E2r L2; tracked GH #24); lurupu-11 (2.045912, unchanged) by a sizer<->renderer creole-lexer divergence (parseCreole leaves unclosed <b>/<font Name> literal, buildStripeAtoms strips them). See ledger.md S1L-b-unicode T1/T2/T3. creole-lexer-unification (2026-07-27) unified the sizer+renderer creole lexers onto one shared StripeSimple.buildLineAtoms helper (sizer dropped parseCreole), and \u2014 scope-expanded \u2014 ported AtomImg's URL cannot-decode text faithfully (creole-atoms.ts cannotDecodeText: http/https raster -> '(Cannot decode: <url>)', .svg url -> '(Cannot decode SVG: <url>)') and fixed a pre-existing description-parser leak of the '[body] as alias' wrapper into node.display for the keyword+bracket form (component-table-containers KEYWORD_RE -> parseBracketDeclaration). Net: lurupu-11 (2.045912->conformant, the original target), pebace-74 (0.172570->conformant, bracket+URL), zotiru-33 (0.914108->conformant) DELETED; nobiza-91 1.460330->0.669271, tuliba-37 6.735899->0.521007, gevozu-46/sunuju-01 4.670->0.611632, vivido-49 2.519868->0.157407, jecici-56 3.182521->0.315278, xufexu-38 1.457690->0.152778, nenedo-78 0.864816->0.168803 all shrank (zero widened). gafico-37/nujito-06 stay pinned unchanged: the T1 spike DISPROVED the brief's premise that the lexer switch would shrink them (their <color>/<u> tags sit adjacent to a decoded <U+000A> where both lexers agree); their residual is the deferred node-c <code> block. Remaining nobiza-91 0.669271 residual = note cannot-decode text measured at NOTE font 13 vs the jar's 14 (separate pre-existing gap; tracked GH #23). Now 112 entries / 351 => 239 (68.1%) conformant. S1L-c (2026-07-28) ported the interface `hideText` leaf dimension: EntityImageDescription.java:137 sets `hideText = symbol == USymbols.INTERFACE` and :209-211 then builds `asSmall` from EMPTY name/desc/stereo, so an interface/circle leaf measures the bare CircleInterface2 square (radius 8 + margin 1 = 18px = 0.25in) regardless of its label -- the label is drawn OUTSIDE the node, and when the shield is not suppressed `getShield` reserves room for it as HTML-table margins rather than by growing the node. Our port had been sizing these as generic text boxes (leaf-sizing.ts#measureLeafNode, new INTERFACE_CIRCLE_SIZE case). That fix UNMASKED a separate pre-existing parser gap that it also closes: a bare quoted `\"Display\" as Alias` line (no type keyword) is CommandCreateElementFull's DISPLAY2/CODE2 branch with SYMBOL omitted, which java:272-275 resolves to actorStyle().toUSymbol() -- an ACTOR, which then makes DescriptionDiagram.isUsecase() true so every remaining STILL_UNKNOWN leaf mutes to actor too. RE_BARE_QUOTED_DECL only admitted the no-alias form, so xacaxe-43-bupe002's five leaves fell to interface and WIDENED 0.555556 -> 1.295833 under the sizing fix; with the `as` clause added they are all exact. Net: 239 -> 272 / 351 (68.1 -> 77.5 pct) conformant, zero widened, 33 entries DELETED, 2 shrank (cukafa-49 0.361111->0.305556, zosuje-43 0.222222->0.146702). The interface-shield bucket is now EMPTY. Two fixtures that bucket carried were misattributions, both corrected in scripts/measure-description-size-deltas.ts CAUSE_PATTERNS: turasu-73-zoni468 is a SPRITE fixture (the sprite regex lacked '/', so every stdlib '<$bundle/name>' fell through to the interface catch) -> S1L-f; cukafa-49-fona812 + gogamo-72-pibo470 are a per-element FONT skinparam gap ('skinparam componentFontSize 18' never reaches measureLeafNode -- fontSpec is one diagram-wide value, with no per-USymbol resolution) -> new S1L-h. Now 79 entries / 351 => 272 (77.5 pct) conformant. S1L-f part 1 (2026-07-28) -- ENGINE MISROUTING, not sprite sizing. `skinparam <selector><<stereo>> {` failed BOTH block-open regexes and fell through to RE_SKINPARAM_LINE, which read the key as `rectangle<<stereo>>` and the VALUE as `{`: the opener was consumed, no block opened, and the body LEAKED into the diagram as content. Every awslib/tupadr3 sprite include ends in an `AWSEntityColoring(x)`-style `!definelong` expanding to exactly that block, so kofuca-08-pafi749 accumulated 53 orphan `BackgroundColor`/`BorderColor`/`}` lines ahead of its real content -- burying the element declarations past descriptive-keywords.ts's SCAN_LINE_LIMIT, so hasDescriptiveElement returned false and dispatcher.ts#resolve fell back to the block's detected type, handing an AWS deployment diagram to the CLASS engine, which measured each node's raw `<img data:image/png;base64,...>` markup as label text (19214px vs the jar's 142px). Fixed in preprocessor.ts (scoped selector-block regex + stereotype appended AFTER the entry name, matching upstream's `param.name() + suffix + stereotype` concatenation). kofuca-08 478.939757 -> 0.305903 (1566x); its residual, and all of ruziru-69-xixo434 / bootstrap-0 (0.682747, correctly routed, ellipse shapes matching), is now GENUINE sprite-dimension resolution -- bundle sprites (`<$bi-globe>`, `,scale=2.5`) contribute no dims (node b measures 23.5x20 vs the jar's 69.5x56.8). That is the remaining S1L-f core. S1L-a (2026-07-28) ported the folder-family leaf: `folder` and `package` are ONE class, USymbolFolder(sname, showTitle) (USymbols.java:79/86), whose asSmall dimension is getMargin().addDimension(dimName.mergeTB(dimStereo, dimLabel)) with getMargin() = [30, 23] and dimName = showTitle ? title.calculateDimension() : FIXED XDimension2D(40, 15). mergeTB takes the MAX width and the SUM of heights, so for `folder` the fixed tab FLOORS the width as well as adding 15 to the height -- a floor this port lacked entirely (`folder b` measured 37.79 vs the jar's 70.00 = max(40, 7.79) + 30; it only bites on a SHORT name, which is why no fixture caught it). For `package` the title is the element CODE and the label carries the display only when the two differ, and the shown title contributes a measured +12px (FOLDER_SHOWN_TITLE_EXTRA_WIDTH -- exact at three widths, deltas 11.999996/11.999976/12.000008; NOT attributable to a single upstream expression, see the constant's own doc). Verified against the jar on all five forms: `package \"a b c d e f g\"` 91.787x37, `package pp as \"Display Here\"` 106.387x51, `package \"Disp Two\" as dd` 84.600x51, `folder \"x\"` 70.000x52, `folder ff as \"Folder Display\"` 115.750x52 -- all exact. 272 -> 279/351 (77.5 -> 79.5 pct), zero widened. NOTE: measureFolderLeaf must keep applying opts.minimumWidth -- omitting it regressed zotiru-33-legi180 (S1L-g's `<style> package { MinimumWidth }` consumer) 0 -> 3.038715 before the floor was threaded back in. The package-folder-tab bucket is now EMPTY: its last two fixtures were misattributions the heuristic made on a leading `artifact`/`package` keyword, both re-bucketed in CAUSE_PATTERNS -- codabo-50-mupa164 is CREOLE TITLED SEPARATORS (`--title1--`/`==title2==` draw a rule carrying their title text, so they contribute the TITLE's width 37.6px, not the raw markup's 62.5px; every other node in that fixture is exact) and tajadu-40-juro990 is a MULTI-LINE QUOTED DISPLAY (upstream's CommandCreateElementMultilines joins the continuation lines; we stop at the first, leaving the id literally `foo2 as \"This artifact` -- its other three nodes are exact). S1L-d (2026-07-28) wired `skinparam wrapWidth` into the SIZER. Fission (the Neutron word-wrap) was ALREADY ported and ALREADY used by the leaf RENDERER (EntityImageDescriptionSupport.ts#buildWrappedLines); leaf-sizing.ts simply never called it, so a wrapped diagram measured its boxes at the unwrapped single-line width while the renderer drew them wrapped -- the same sizer<->renderer divergence family as creole-lexer-unification. New leaf-sizing-text.ts#measureTextBlock reuses getSplitted (never re-derives the break positions), threaded via ClassifyCtx.wrapWidth -> BoxSizingOpts.wrapWidth; maxWidth 0 (upstream's own default -- it sets PName.MaximumWidth nowhere) delegates to the unwrapped helpers unchanged, so this is zero-diff for every diagram that does not set the skinparam. Wiring it made mejoxi-96-cegu294's HEIGHTS exact immediately (58/72) with widths still 4.9875 short, which isolated a SECOND, independent bug in the same fixture: the `[\"...\"]` bracket shorthand was stripping quotes that upstream KEEPS. Upstream's eventuallyRemoveStartingAndEndingDoubleQuote (java:311) sees the display with its brackets still attached, so it no-ops and the bracket wrapper comes off afterwards -- our parseBracketDeclaration passed the ALREADY unbracketed body through stripFullWrap. Jar-verified: `[plain]` draws plain, `[\"quoted\"]` draws \"quoted\", while `component \"cq\"` and `component cq2 as \"dq\"` do strip. (The 4.9875 was one `\"` glyph; unwrapped the gap was exactly twice that, both quotes on one line.) mejoxi-96 now exact at 238.100x58 / 238.362x72. 279 -> 280/351 (79.5 -> 79.8 pct), zero widened; the wrapWidth bucket is EMPTY. S1L-f part 2a (2026-07-28), four fixes that each unmasked the next. (1) SPRITE SCALE: `CommandCreoleSprite.java:82` scales a creole `<$name>` by `Parser.getScale(...) * fc.getSize2D() / 13.0` -- the requested scale TIMES the ambient font size over a 13px reference -- and it applies to EVERY sprite kind, since the factor lives in the creole command, not in any Sprite class. This port used the raw registry dims * requested scale, i.e. silently assumed font 13. Jar-verified at two sizes and two kinds: a 48x48 encoded sprite measures 51.6923 at font 14 and 96.0 at font 26; a 16x16 SVG sprite 17.2308 and 32.0. New `spriteScale` in creole-atoms-measure.ts (creole-atoms.ts was split at the 500-line cap); both RENDER sites now thread their own font so drawn and measured sprite geometry cannot drift. (2) PER-ATOM FONTS: the sizer concatenated every text atom and measured the result at the BASE font, which is exact only while every atom shares that size -- wrong for a `==heading` line (`fontConfigurationForHeading`: order 0 -> +4, 1 -> +2, 2 -> +1) or a `<size:N>` run. `buildLineAtoms` already returns atoms under their own cascaded fonts (the renderer's `measureAtomsWidthHeight` had always summed per-atom), so `lineTextMetrics` now does the same. (3) STEREOTYPE IN A QUOTED DISPLAY: `parseNameSection` rejoined the quoted display before scanning for decoration, so guillemets INSIDE the quotes were extracted as a stereotype AND left in the display -- reserving one extra stereotype line (+lineH) plus STEREO_MARGIN (+2). Upstream's STEREOTYPE group sits after the CODE/DISPLAY alternatives, so it can only match after the closing quote. (4) GUILLEMET: `CreoleParser.java:175` runs `skinParam.guillemet().manageGuillemet(line)` before stripes are built, so `<<x>>` in DISPLAY text draws as the two glyphs `\u00abx\u00bb`, not four literal chars -- 17.3px too wide per occurrence here. Ported to core/text/Guillemet.ts and threaded through BOTH the sizer (ClassifyCtx -> BoxSizingOpts) and the renderer (buildTextBlock), honouring `skinparam guillemet` (mogidu-85-roxe269 sets `none`). Net: 280 -> 284/351 (79.8 -> 80.9 pct), zero widened. nenedo-78-fiva569 drove all four: 6 of its 8 nodes are now exact. Class ratchet unmoved (219/708, zero widened); class/component/usecase structure 708/262/90 all still 100 pct EQUAL. Five unit expectations that had encoded the missing /13 (and one toBe->toBeCloseTo for per-atom summation's ~1e-14 association drift) were corrected. STILL OPEN for S1L-f part 2b: SVG-form sprites (`sprite N <svg ...>`) are not parsed at all -- bootstrap AND archimate are both SVG-sprite bundles, so ruziru-69/bootstrap-0/tatori-66/sprite-SVG-fill-management-3/turasu-73 still measure their sprites as 0. S1L-f part 2b (2026-07-28) ported SVG-form sprites. `sprite N <svg ...>` (CommandSpriteSvg, single-line) and its multi-line form (CommandSpriteSvgMultiline, END = a line ending `</svg>`) were not in the grammar at all -- only the encoded `[WxH/Nz]` forms were -- so bootstrap AND archimate, which are BOTH SVG-sprite bundles, registered nothing and every `<$name>` from them measured 0. New core/klimt/sprite/SpriteSvg.ts carries `UImageSvg#getData`'s dimension rule exactly: a viewBox WINS outright (width = its 3rd number, height its 4th, each Math.ceil'd), else the `width=`/`height=` attribute inside the `<svg ...>` tag read as leading digits. That precedence is why archimate's `width=\"19.995mm\"` never needs unit handling -- its viewBox supplies the number. getSpriteMonochrome now DECLINES an SVG sprite (it was an unchecked cast) and render-atoms.ts re-emits the element as an image/svg+xml data URI, untinted (upstream's SpriteSvg ignores fontColor/forcedColor too). descriptive-keywords.ts strips SVG sprite regions from the dispatch scan window as well -- bootstrap is ~7200 lines of them, the same burial that made stripSpriteRegions necessary for the encoded form. Also closed the gap measureUsecase's own doc comment had flagged (\"no corpus fixture exercises a tall atom inside a use-case label\"): the ellipse footprint now includes atomHeightBonus on the HEIGHT axis, not just the width. 284 -> 286/351 (80.9 -> 81.5 pct), zero widened; tatori-66-kaci883 + sprite-SVG-fill-management-3 (the two inline-SVG fixtures) are CONFORMANT. leaf-sizing.ts was split again at the 500-line cap into leaf-sizing-consts.ts + leaf-sizing-folder.ts. OPEN, precisely characterised: ruziru-69-xixo434/bootstrap-0 still miss because a sprite's USE-CASE footprint is not always its box. Jar-measured: `bi-globe` at scale 2.5 measures 43.077 inside a RECTANGLE but only 39.642 inside a USECASE, while `bi-bootstrap-fill` measures 43.077 in BOTH -- same declared `<svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\">`, same scale, both syntaxes (`,scale=` and `{scale=}`) agreeing. So the ellipse path uses something CONTENT-dependent, most likely SvgNanoParser's drawn-ink bounds rather than the declared box. Porting that is an SVG path-bbox subsystem -- its own mission, NOT a divergence. S1L-k (2026-07-28) ported the sprite INK footprint. A use-case ellipse is NOT fit to the text block's declared dimension: `TextBlockInEllipse`'s ctor takes only `alpha` from `text.calculateDimension()`, then calls `Footprint#getEllipse(text, alpha)`, which DRAWS the block onto a point-collecting UGraphic; a drawn path contributes just its min/max corners (Footprint.java:147-150). Those corners come from `UPath#addInternal` (UPath.java:82-94), which records ONLY the endpoint of a SEG_ARCTO and EVERY coordinate pair -- Bezier control points included -- of everything else. So the box is the CONTROL-POLYGON box; a true-extrema box would be wrong here, and no curve flattening is needed. New core/klimt/sprite/svg-path-bbox.ts implements exactly that rule (command coverage per `SvgPath#toUPath`, with H/V and the S/T reflections normalised inline), and SpriteSvg now carries inkWidth/inkHeight alongside its declared box. This explains the finding S1L-f left open: `bi-globe` and `bi-bootstrap-fill` BOTH declare `<svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\">`, but bi-globe's outer circle is an ARC (endpoint only), so it inks 16x13.846 while bi-bootstrap-fill inks the full 16x16 -- hence 69.458x56.766 vs 74.957x61.165 at scale 2.5, from identical declarations. Verified: our computed ink boxes match the hand-derived numbers exactly, and 5 of ruziru-69's 6 nodes are now EXACT (b/c/d/e/f). ruziru-69-xixo434 + bootstrap-0 shrank 0.124042 -> 0.069047; 286/351 (81.5 pct) holds, zero widened, class ratchet unmoved. RESIDUAL, NOT SOLVED: node `a` of both fixtures is a MIXED sprite+text display (`\"<$bi-globe>\\nbi-globe\"`), ours 73.965x48.558 vs the jar's 66.026x43.587. A mixed block's footprint depends on where each shape is actually DRAWN -- `Footprint#drawText` offsets by `dim.getHeight() - 1.5`, and a sprite's ink sits at an OFFSET inside its declared line box (bi-globe's ink starts 1.077 units down) -- so a per-line max/sum model cannot express it. Back-solving the jar's numbers did not reconcile with either candidate model, so this is left DIAGNOSED-BUT-OPEN rather than guessed: closing it means modelling Footprint's actual point collection with draw positions. S1L-k residual CLOSED (2026-07-28) by porting the real ellipse fit. `TextBlockInEllipse` takes only `alpha` from the DECLARED dimension, then calls `Footprint#getEllipse`, and `ContainingEllipse` maps `y -> y/alpha` and takes the SMALLEST ENCLOSING CIRCLE of the collected points: width = 2r, height = 2r*alpha. The old closed form (diag = sqrt(W^2 + (H/alpha)^2) over the bounding box) is exactly right for two opposite corners or a rectangle's four -- which is why every text-only and sprite-only fixture matched it -- but wrong for a MIXED block, where the fit also becomes ORDER-DEPENDENT (jar: `\"<$bi-globe>\\nbi-globe\"` = 66.026x43.587 vs `\"bi-globe\\n<$bi-globe>\"` = 69.791x45.945, same lines swapped). Two positional details were derived, not fitted: a TEXT run's collected box is `[y + ypos - h + 1.5, y + ypos + 1.5]` where `Footprint#drawText` applies the -(h-1.5) shift and `AtomText#drawU` draws at `ypos = height - descent` with `StringBounder#getDescent` defaulting to `size / 4.5` (at 14 -> 10.888..., so the box starts 1.611 ABOVE its line top -- that asymmetry is what makes order matter); and a SPRITE contributes its INK box at its own OFFSET inside the declared line box. A numeric scan independently landed on 10.9 before the /4.5 constant was found, which confirmed it. Verified against the jar on SEVEN shapes (sprite; text; text x2; sprite+text; text+sprite; sprite+text x2; sprite x2) to within 5e-4 px. Stereotype lines are merged ABOVE the label before the fit (EntityImageUseCase.java:96-109) and so contribute points too -- mopimi-10-jaco443/lunexo-59-fupo775 are entirely stereotyped use-cases and were the proof. One more over-reach fixed en route, same class as S1L-f's stereotype bug but through a different path: `stripUrl` removed a `[[url]]` from INSIDE a quoted display. Upstream's `UrlBuilder.OPTIONAL` is anchored AFTER the CODE/DISPLAY alternatives, so inside the quotes `[[...]]` is ordinary Creole link content; stripping it dropped real display text (bivira-53 lost a whole URL, and its sibling lost a sprite NESTED in one). stripUrl is now quote-aware. Net: 286 -> 291/351 (81.5 -> 82.9 pct), zero widened; ruziru-69-xixo434 + bootstrap-0 CONFORMANT (the S1L-k target). Class ratchet unmoved (219/708); structure 100 pct EQUAL on all three types. S1L-e batch 1 (2026-07-28) -- three DISPLAY-PARSE bugs, not cluster geometry. The container-cluster bucket is a first-match heuristic that tags any fixture with a container keyword opening `{`, so it had collected these. (1) NOTE newlines: `emitNoteLeaf` passed the note text straight through as the display, so `note left: a\\nb\\nc` measured as ONE line -- berufi-69-dara369's note came out 447.24x23 against the jar's 194.39x49. Upstream routes every note's text through `Display.getWithNewlines`. Fixed four fixtures at a stroke (berufi-69, bobije-35, seline-83, xoculo-95 all shared the IDENTICAL 3.1839 delta -- an identical delta across fixtures is a reliable tell for one shared cause). (2) LINK-ENDPOINT newlines: `ensureEndpoint` built its node as `makeNode(ep.id, ep.id, ...)`, so an endpoint declared inline (`Kurier -- (Transport der Sendung\\nEP: ...)`) used the RAW id as its display; `getDummy` runs the display through getWithNewlines while `quark.getName()` stays raw -- the same id/display split `finalizeDisplay` already documents. fepuvo-06-rugi981 6.27in -> 2.89in. (3) MULTI-LINE BRACKET OPEN: `ELEMENT_MULTILINE_OPEN_RE`'s colour alternative was `#\\\\w+`, which cannot match a full spec, so `node B #red|green;line.dashed;line:blue [` failed the pattern entirely and fell through to KEYWORD_RE -- which swallowed the spec AND the trailing `[` into the element's NAME (titona-45-jile471 3.50in vs the jar's 0.82in; balomu-94-kegi822 2.818 -> 0.194). Now uses the same character class `RE_COLOR` does. Net: 291 -> 297/351 (82.9 -> 84.6 pct), zero widened; container-cluster 30 -> 24. S1L-e batch 2 (2026-07-28): the `USymbolSimpleAbstract` family. `control`, `entity` and `boundary` extend USymbolSimpleAbstract, the SAME class as actor and interface, so their `asSmall` STACKS a fixed drawing above the label (`mergeLayoutT12B3(stereo, drawing, label)`) -- width = max(drawing, label), height = drawing + label -- rather than wrapping text in a bordered box. This port had no case for them, so they fell to `measureBox`'s generic [20,20] margin: `control \"C\"` measured 30x34 against the jar's 32x46. Drawing dims are each shape's own `calculateDimension`, all `radius*2 + 2*margin` with margin 4 / radius 12: Control 32x32 (svek/Control.java:51-53,:87-88), EntityDomain 32x32 (:50-52,:75), Boundary 24 + left 17 + 8 = 49 wide x 32 (:52-55,:98). `interface`/`circle` stay excluded -- same family, but `hideText` drops the label so they size as the bare circle (S1L-c). 297 -> 300/351 (84.6 -> 85.5 pct), zero widened; container-cluster 24 -> 22. TRIAGE of the remaining 22 (by source signal, recorded so the next pass does not re-derive it): 2 are the UNIMPLEMENTED creole `{{ }}` embedded sub-diagram (kovaxi-11-reti348, zidebi-71-nocu387 -- already ledgered under A3), 4 are sprite, 1 is per-element font (jecici-56-bimu826 sets `skinparam rectangleFontSize 10` -> S1L-h), and the other ~15 carry no other signal and are the genuine `computeContainerBbox` core. Several of those share IDENTICAL deltas in pairs (0.2083, 0.1944, 0.1667, 0.1082, 0.0833), which has twice now been a reliable tell for ONE shared cause per pair rather than N problems. S1L-e batch 3 (2026-07-28): EMPTY displays. An empty `[ ]` element body draws a box of PURE MARGIN. Two independent bugs conspired to give it a text line's worth of height. (1) `finishElementBlock` only assigned the display `if (body.length > 0)`, so an empty body left the element's CODE standing in as its label -- upstream sets the display from the block unconditionally, with no fall-back-to-the-code branch. (2) `lineCount('')` returned 1, billing a zero-length display a 14px line; an empty display has NO lines (a display of one SPACE is still a line -- only zero length is empty). Jar-verified directly: `component c [ ]` draws NO text at all and boxes at 40x30 (margin + icon only) while a plain `component d` is 47.787x44. A unit test had PINNED the old behaviour ('an empty body keeps the code as the display'); it carried no jar citation, unlike its siblings, and was an assumption -- corrected with the measurement above rather than flipped silently. 300 -> 306/351 (85.5 -> 87.2 pct), zero widened; container-cluster 22 -> 16. Also re-triaged: the `<style> component { FontSize 19 }` path is per-element FONT (S1L-h), NOT cluster geometry -- 4 more of this bucket (fasave-91-jaka816, zonobi-55-zuna105, zosuje-43-zebi775, loroto-06-fano471) plus jecici-56's `skinparam rectangleFontSize`. The cause classifier only matches the `skinparam` spelling, so the `<style>` spelling lands here. S1L-h is therefore worth ~7 fixtures, not 2. S1L-h (2026-07-28): per-element FONT reaches the sizer. `resolveElementFontSize(theme, sname, 'title')` already existed and the RENDERER already called it (`renderer-symbol.ts#textFont`) -- only the sizer never did, the same lock-step gap as wrapWidth and the creole lexer. Threaded `ClassifyCtx.fontSizeFor` -> `BoxSizingOpts.fontSize`, resolved ONCE at the top of `measureLeafNode` so every per-symbol rule inherits it. Only the SIZE is threaded: `glyphWidth` ignores the family (`_fontName`), so FontName/FontStyle are width-neutral under the deterministic width table. Note the bucket UNDERSTATED this: the cause classifier only matches the `skinparam <el>FontSize` spelling, so the `<style> <el> { FontSize N }` spelling was landing in container-cluster -- 9 fixtures carry a per-element font declaration, not the 2 labelled element-font. One nested gap had to be fixed with it, jar-verified: an `<img>` CANNOT-DECODE fallback run is drawn at the DIAGRAM-DEFAULT font, NOT the element's -- `<img:x/y.svg>` alone measures 100.362x14 identically with and without `skinparam rectangleFontSize 10`, and